1:1 COMMENT "# generator_bidirectional.z -- a generator that receives values back"
1:69 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "# from the caller."
2:19 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "#"
3:2 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# `call`'s parameter list declares the PER-CALL INPUT: at most one,"
4:68 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# and what it declares is the input's type, its ownership, and the"
5:67 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# label its call sites read. Inside the body, `name: yield v` yields"
6:69 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# `v` and binds `name` to whatever the call that RESUMES it supplies"
7:69 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# -- so a first yield written in expression form reads the SECOND"
8:66 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# `.call`'s value, not the first's. The generator yields before it"
9:67 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# can receive, which is why the input is not a binding made on entry."
10:70 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "#"
11:2 EOL "\n"
12:1 COMMENT "# The for-loop only drives generators that receive nothing; one with"
12:69 EOL "\n"
13:1 COMMENT "# an input is driven by hand through `with` and `.call`. See"
13:61 EOL "\n"
14:1 COMMENT "# doc/spec.pdoc Generator functions."
14:37 EOL "\n"
15:1 EOL "\n"
16:1 COMMENT "# Emits the first two integers unconditionally, then asks the caller"
16:69 EOL "\n"
17:1 COMMENT "# whether to emit a third. The caller's decision arrives on the"
17:64 EOL "\n"
18:1 COMMENT "# second `.call`, and the expression-form yield binds it to `keep`."
18:68 EOL "\n"
